@andrewlewis there is another place that we call `releaseAdsLoader` and I just wanted to run it by you and see if this case could also cause issues. 
We call `releaseAdsLoader` when we're going to start a new video and the new one has a different preroll tag than the previous one:
```
    private suspend fun wrapMediaSourceWithAds(context: Context, mediaSource: MediaSource, _prerollTag: String?): MediaSource {
        val adTagUri = Uri.parse(_prerollTag.orEmpty())

        if (adTagUri != loadedAdTagUri) {
            /** HERE! Could this call cause a crash too? **/ 
            releaseAdsLoader()
            loadedAdTagUri = adTagUri
        }
 
        val formattedAdTag = processAdTag(_prerollTag) 

        if (adsLoader == null) {
            adsLoader = createAdsLoader(context)
        }

        val adsLoaderInstance = adsLoader ?: return mediaSource
        adsLoaderInstance.setPlayer(player)

        // Compose the content media source into a new AdsMediaSource with both ads and content.
        val dataSpec = DataSpec(formattedAdTag.asUri())
        val adsMediaSource = AdsMediaSource(mediaSource, dataSpec, dataSpec.uri, this, adsLoaderInstance, adViewProvider)
        adsMediaSource.addEventListener(mainHandler, this)
        return adsMediaSource
    }
```

releasePlayer() is not called in this case, but I just want to be on the safe side.
